# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestDrainWithoutFence. A drain that waits instead of fencing: the
# close records the allocator head without raising the initiator's entry, so a
# write admitted before the close and delivered after it is allocated above the
# recorded head. Waiting for every admitted write to return is the same thing
# here: a call returns by timeout while its append is still delivered. It is also
# a close taken while the initiator's view of the gate is closed, which cannot
# bump.
MODULE: HandOffBoundDrainWithoutFence
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the close records the head without fencing out writes admitted before it
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ fEpoch' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ \E h \in CloseHeads : hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, h)
--- REPLACE
    /\ fEpoch' = fEpoch + 1
\* MUTATION: no fence: the shard's entry for the initiator is not raised.
    /\ fFence' = fFence
    /\ \E h \in CloseHeads : hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, h)
--- END
